  "refuter_findings": [
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:10:1",
      "id": "thm-mod-two-cohomology-of-bo-n",
      "location": "step 2.1",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "Step 2.1 states: 'the fiber of p^*\\gamma_{n-1} over (W,v) is W\\cap v^{\\perp}. Therefore, by [F7], $w_j(\\pi^*\\gamma_n)=w_j(L)w_j(p^*\\gamma_{n-1})=w_j(p^*\\gamma_{n-1})=p^*w_j(\\gamma_{n-1})$ for every $j$, since a trivial line bundle has total class $1$.' The middle equality misapplies the Whitney formula: the correct expansion of the split bundle $\\pi^*\\gamma_n\\cong L\\oplus p^*\\gamma_{n-1}$ is $w_j(\\pi^*\\gamma_n)=\\sum_{i=0}^{j}w_i(L)w_{j-i}(p^*\\gamma_{n-1})$, so the term $w_1(L)p^*w_{j-1}(\\gamma_{n-1})$ (and further terms for larger $j$) is dropped. The claim is false, not merely under-justified: take $n=j=2$. Since $w_2(p^*\\gamma_1)=0$ by the rank convention, step 2.1 asserts $w_2(\\pi^*\\gamma_2)=p^*w_2(\\gamma_1)=0$, whereas the true value is $w_2(\\pi^*\\gamma_2)=w_1(L)p^*w_1(\\gamma_1)\\neq0$: $w_1(L)$ spans $\\ker\\eta$ in degree $1$ (the Gysin short exact sequences of step 4.1 with $e_2(\\gamma_1)=w_1(\\gamma_1)=a\\neq0$ by [F6]), so it is not in the image of $p^*$, while $p^*w_1(\\gamma_1)\\neq0$; their product is nonzero by the Leray-Hirsch freeness of $H^*(S(\\gamma_2);\\mathbb F_2)$ over $H^*(BO(1);\\mathbb F_2)$ with basis $\\{1,u\\}$ used in step 1.2. Step 3.1's assertion '$\\eta(w_j(\\gamma_n))=w_j(\\gamma_{n-1})$ for every $j$' and the decomposition in step 6.1 both rest on this step. The conclusion survives only after restricting indices: for $j\\le n-1$ one has $w_{j-1}(\\gamma_{n-1})=0$, so the corrected identity gives $\\eta(w_j(\\gamma_n))=w_j(\\gamma_{n-1})$ on exactly the range the induction uses, while the $j=n$ instance of the stated equality is false.",
      "severity": "nonfatal",
      "observed_sha256": "a974db982645df27a2512e7e4bcf4fefbcdcb865c773c57bab86e485e3460c3e"
    }
  ],
